@snail_smoothie2314 It’s fair to care about workers’ conditions — but this concern should be consistent across the entire global garment industry, not only when it involves Shein.
Many affordable clothes sold in developed countries like in Target are made in Vietnam, Turkey, or Bangladesh, where average garment wages are often lower than in China. Yet people rarely raise the same concerns about those supply chains.
If we truly care about workers, the discussion should be about improving standards everywhere, not singling out one country or company.

