@VioletRaven.  While all of that is true the original comment is not talking about high end brand names. This person isn't telling you to just buy expensive, this person is trying to tell people who feel forced to buy fast fashion that you can get better quality and more value for your money. 

Fast fashion is easy, affordable and convenient from the outside. However in reality it is none of those things, the pieces from shein are so poorly made from horrible fabric it gets ruined much much faster than other fast fashion brands. You will be paying more overtime to replace ruined and old clothes. It appears more convenient to keep buying pieces than finding better quality on second-hand sites or thrift stores but its just costing you more and more money over time. 

People need to research what they're buying, where they are buying from and budget appropriately so they can actually wear clothes that will last them at least a few years.  You can shop certain fast fashion brands responsibly by checking the fabric, the fit and reviews.

@VioletRaven.  I have also had shein in the past, and it has fallen apart for me especially sweaters and skirts. its not just the fact it could fall apart, the quality of the fabric makes it difficult to wash and isn't great for the skin and thats on top of the working conditions and many other issues.

