@dw620 What you said is not true, what you said about workers from other countries is true, not for China. It is the Chinese people's sense of responsibility for their families, hoping that their children and parents can live better than themselves, and are willing to sacrifice themselves. Most of the workers in this urban village in Guangzhou come from Hubei and are self-employed. Self employment costs 500 yuan per day, which means that the working hours are 10-14 hours and the labor market is free at 11 pm every night. Indeed, they live in a very difficult situation, living in a house that costs 500 yuan per month, eating takeout for 15 yuan per meal, cooking for 500-700 yuan per month, and spending very little money on themselves. Usually, couples working in the same industry can save 200000 (approximately 30000 US dollars) a year for their families. Building a new house in a rural area with free land, the construction cost is 700 yuan per square meter for the first floor and 500 yuan per square meter for the second floor and above, plus ordinary decoration. Each floor is 100 square meters, with 4 floors, totaling 400000 yuan for the entire building. Buying a house for the child to get married in a county town costs 400000 to 800000 yuan. The average price of new commercial housing in Chinese cities is 10300 yuan per square meter, while most county towns only have a few thousand yuan per square meter. It is normal for the price to be 3000+-6000+yuan per square meter. Buy a car for your child, maybe Audi, as China usually accounts for 30% of the global sales of these luxury brands. It is not surprising that these worker couples can contribute tens of thousands of savings (RMB 300K-900K).
