@Laura-gd4ku Absolutely this.

Political action, like supporting laws that hold corporations accountable and doing things thst support labor unionization everywhere, is infinitely more effective than any personal lifestyle change. After all, capitalist hegemony *wants* us all to feel personally guilty for its wrongdoings; the individualization of responsibility for exploitation is one of the oldest tactics in the corporate playbook, as is selling the solutions to the problems they create, which is what happens when they turn right back around and sell us "sustainable" products even as they maintain financial stakes in the global slave market.

The way forward will never be in shame, nor in sacrifice, but rather in solidarity. If there is no ethical consumption under capitalism, we should oppose the cause of suffering - capitalism, rather than focusing on a symptom - consumption.

