@crunchycandyzombie6455 Recognizing that markets are complex and that consumer demand is indeed one of the many forces driving business decisions is just necessary. Granted, consumers are not as important anymore, but you cannot deny that there is a portion of influence, as little as it is. If everything was already a monopoly, there would not be any use for marketing campaigns, for example. 

No one here is saying that this alone will solve any issue - after all, it has systemic causes as you know. But given that one can choose between a harmful option and a less harmful option, I'd argue one should choose the less harmful one.
We can both shop from the least shitty sources AND have our skulls cracked during a strike. One can be anti-capitalist and recognize that, yes, "there is no ethical consumption under capitalism", but there are less and more unethical consumption.

